GHC 6.2.2 -- mhs: pre-FFI-addendum foreign declarations modernised
The tree still carries the 1999 FFI syntax in places: `foreign import
"name" unsafe f`, `foreign import ccall "name" unsafe f` (safety after
the entity string), `foreign label`. MicroHs implements the Haskell 98 FFI
addendum: calling convention first, safety before the entity string, and
`foreign import ccall "&sym"` for a label. Rewritten in CompManager,
ObjLink, DriverFlags, SysTools (its private rawSystem, active because we
compile with __GLASGOW_HASKELL__=408), ByteCodeItbls (nine RTS entry
labels) and eight ilxGen test programs. The C side is unchanged.

